  faqs: [
    { question: "How does a family in Bhilwara actually go about finding an IB tutor?", answer: "It starts with the specifics: programme, subject, level, and the exam sitting your child is working toward. IB Gram uses that to shortlist tutors who have genuinely taught the exact course, since Bhilwara has no confirmed IB school of its own to search around. A free trial lesson comes before anything gets decided." },
    { question: "Can IB Gram arrange an IGCSE tutor in Bhilwara for Cambridge or Edexcel?", answer: "Yes, for either board, and it runs as online home tuition rather than a doorstep visit. A student is matched by the precise code and tier, Cambridge 0580 Extended or an equivalent Edexcel specification, using that board's own past papers, building toward whichever series the school has actually entered the student for." },
    { question: "Will a tutor actually come to our house in Bhilwara?", answer: "No. Door-to-door lessons exist only in Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR; everywhere else, Bhilwara included, a lesson runs as a live video call, one to one, with a shared digital whiteboard standing in for a physical one. That is genuinely delivered to your child's own desk, just never by someone knocking on your door." },
    { question: "What's a realistic budget for an IB or IGCSE tutor in Bhilwara?", answer: "There is no single number; it moves with the programme, level, subject, session length and how recently the tutor has taught that exact course, with Diploma HL work usually at the higher end. The trial costs nothing, a figure gets proposed alongside the match, and nothing locks a family in once regular sessions start." },
    { question: "Does any school in Bhilwara actually teach IB or IGCSE?", answer: "Not one we can independently confirm. Sangam School of Excellence, on the Chittorgarh bypass at Atun, shows up on some directories as an IB or Cambridge school, but its own official site states CBSE affiliation only, with no international programme currently running. Bhilwara families pursuing IB or IGCSE typically do so through tutoring, or by boarding at a school elsewhere, Jaipur being the most common choice." },
    { question: "Is the first lesson genuinely free, or is there a catch?", answer: "Genuinely free. A tutor teaches one real topic from the actual syllabus, at no cost, before a family commits to anything. If it goes well, a short written plan for the first month follows, setting out what gets taught and how you will hear about progress." },
    { question: "How far will a tutor go in helping with an IB Internal Assessment?", answer: "Up to a clear line: guidance yes, drafting no. That covers narrowing a research question down to something workable, explaining what a criterion is actually looking for, sanity-checking a data-collection plan, and marking a draft the student has written themselves. Producing the assessed text, or substantially rewriting it, breaches IB's academic integrity rules and is simply not something a tutor here will do." },
    { question: "Which Diploma subjects does IB Gram actually cover for a Bhilwara student?", answer: "The spread matches what a small Diploma cohort here typically studies: both Maths routes at HL and SL, the three sciences, Economics, Business Management, English A, Computer Science, plus support around Theory of Knowledge and the Extended Essay. A less common subject combination still gets matched, just from a narrower field of specialists." },
    { question: "Is MYP or PYP tutoring available in Bhilwara, or only Diploma support?", answer: "The full continuum is covered. MYP tutoring for a Bhilwara student usually focuses on criterion-based writing across the sciences and Individuals and Societies, and on shaping the Personal Project ahead of its Year 5 checkpoint. PYP-age children get shorter, more frequent sessions built around reading, number sense and early research habits." },
    { question: "With no local IB school, does online tutoring genuinely work for Bhilwara students?", answer: "It tends to work well here, arguably better than the alternative, given Bhilwara has neither a local school nor a tutor base built around these syllabuses. A shared screen, live worked examples and a session recording to revisit cover most of what sitting beside a tutor would offer, while opening up specialists a single city's supply simply could not." },
    { question: "How thoroughly are IB Gram's tutors actually checked before being introduced?", answer: "Qualifications get reviewed, along with how recently a tutor has taught the precise subject and level in question, and how they handle Internal Assessment guidance. With no Bhilwara school anchoring a local pool, recent, hands-on syllabus experience counts for more than a broad but dated IB background. The trial lesson lets a family confirm the rest directly." },
    { question: "At what point should a Bhilwara student start IB or IGCSE tutoring?", answer: "Starting when the course itself begins works best, Class 11 for the Diploma and Grade 9 for IGCSE, leaving time to shore up fundamentals before internal exams, IA deadlines and predicted grades all converge. A later start, even in the final year, can still help if sessions concentrate on the highest-value topics instead of chasing full coverage." },
    { question: "My child studies CBSE or RBSE in Bhilwara but wants to switch to IB or IGCSE. Is that doable?", answer: "Fairly often, actually, precisely because no Bhilwara school offers either from the outset. Content is rarely the real obstacle; exam vocabulary is, so command words like 'evaluate' and 'justify' need direct coaching, alongside planning habits IAs and coursework demand, ideally starting the summer before the switch." },
    { question: "What times actually suit Bhilwara families for online sessions?", answer: "Weekday evenings after school and weekend mornings cover most bookings. Timings shift a little earlier through the worst of the summer heat, and sessions flex around whatever break the school calendar sets. Adding a second weekly slot ahead of mocks or an exam series is a minor adjustment, not a big ask." },
    { question: "What happens if the tutor assigned in Bhilwara just isn't the right fit?", answer: "A different one gets found, without fuss. Regular check-ins exist specifically to catch a poor fit early rather than let it drag on, and no contract obliges a family to continue with a tutor who is not delivering. Stopping altogether, at any point, costs nothing extra." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram connected to any Bhilwara school, or to the IB or Cambridge directly?", answer: "No, on every count. IB Gram runs independently, with no partnership, endorsement or representation involving any Bhilwara school, the International Baccalaureate Organization or Cambridge Assessment International Education. Schools named on this page are mentioned only to describe their actual curriculum, and a tutor's planning follows that student's own school calendar and board syllabus." },
  ],

